  "headline_finding": "Stage 0 hard gate passed exactly (105/105 curves). Part A's categorical prediction held with zero exceptions across 480,000 specializations per run (M1=0, M2=1.000 exactly, both runs), and the dual-path cross-check found zero disagreements over 32,000 specializations per run. However, the contract's own cross-curve null control (measured_null_1) FAILED as literally specified -- it did not exhibit the forbidden cycle types the contract required -- which by the contract's own text renders Stage 2 VOID. The Executor's own algebraic explanation (Finding 1) argues the null was mechanism-identical to the treatment (Frobenius sign-flip applies per-point regardless of common curve membership), suggesting the underlying phenomenon may be MORE general than H-MONO-45183a's own derivation claims, not that the categorical result is wrong. Independent review must determine which reading is correct before any disposition. M3 (quantitative split frequency) showed large deviations (sigma up to 24) at m=5 on small-order curves, attributed by the Executor to a disclosed toy-scale birthday-paradox selection-bias mechanism (Finding 2) requiring independent verification.",
